1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,049
Block Party Challenge. A party game made for the creator Dee name, for Hack the Audience.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:13,675
Dee name's shorts are already games. Find the diamond, the greed game, don't say the letter. Every short is a game his viewers can play along with.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,829
And his tagline is: subscribe and join the game. So we let his viewers really join.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,305
One big screen, a stream or a classroom TV, shows a room code and a Q R code.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,155
Everyone joins on their phone. No app, no account. Here, ten players.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,924
Round one, telepathy. Pick the answer most people will pick.

7
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,830
The reveal shows the crowd. You score for every player who agreed with you.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,548
The greed game. A shared pot of coins. Take a few and everyone keeps them. Get greedy together, and everyone gets nothing.

9
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,062
Find the diamond, hidden in a field of blocks. Closer guesses score more.

10
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:12,517
Block telepathy: pick the block the crowd picks.

11
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,825
And his most watched format: don't say it. Name something in one word, but Korean words with the letter rieul, or English words with an E, are busted.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,176
Unique clean words score double. The streamer can tap any word to reject it, and a safety filter hides bad words.

13
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,423
Lava. Stand on a safe block. Stand alone for a bonus.

14
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,144
Every round is timed by the server, so nobody can cheat the clock.

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,959
Then the winner, and every episode feeds a weekly season leaderboard.

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,407
The weekly final is recorded with the game overlay, and becomes his next short. Every day, the top three in the daily challenge win a seat in it.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:19,102
Brands sponsor the episodes and the prizes, so kids never pay to enter. In our base case, that's about fifty million won in year one, with every assumption in the open.

18
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:36,785
And after every episode, one click turns it into a ready-to-edit vertical short: the big moments of each round and the podium, in Korean, with the sponsor credited. Dee name just adds his music and posts.

19
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:47,716
It runs on Cloudflare's edge, one room per durable object. Load tested with three hundred phones in one room, and monitored every five minutes. Built by an autonomous agent studio, Nightshift Labs.

